    "title": "Barcelona vs. Newcastle United Lineups, Predictions, UEFA Champions League Live Streaming, How & Where to Watch",
    "text": "The Champions League Round of 16 returns for the second leg matches this week, and FC Barcelona will play at home when they host Newcastle United.Both teams played each other last week for the first leg at St. James Park. Ahead of the second leg, both teams played in their respective leagues.FC Barcelona played at the Spotify Camp Nou against Sevilla, and they defeated them 5-2 to remain top of the La Liga table. Barcelona's goalscorers were Dani Olmo, Joao Cancelo, and Raphinha, who scored a hat trick.Newcastle United played against Chelsea in the Premier League at Stamford Bridge. Newcastle United won 1-0 with a goal from Anthony Gordon in the first half.Last week, Newcastle United and Barcelona drew 1-1 at St. James' Park. Harvey Barnes scored in the 86th minute, which made fans believe the win was set, but a last-minute penalty goal from Lamine Yamal made it 1-1.Lamine Yamal of FC Barcelona passes the ball whilst under pressure from Lewis Hall of Newcastle United during the UEFA Champions League 2025/26 Round of 16 First Leg match between Newcastle United FC and FC Barcelona at St James' Park on March 10, 2026 in Newcastle upon Tyne, England. (Photo by George Wood/Getty Images)Photo by George Wood/Getty Images (Photo by George Wood&sol;Getty Images)Official Lineups for FC Barcelona and Newcastle UnitedFC BarcelonaGoalkeeper: Joan GarciaDefenders: Joao Cancelo, Gerard Martin, Pau Cubarsi, Eric GarciaMidfielders: Pedri, Marc Bernal, Fermin LopezForwards: Raphinha, Robert Lewandowski, Lamine YamalNewcastle UnitedGoalkeeper: Aaron RamsdaleDefenders: Lewis Hall, Dan Burn, Malick Thiaw, Kieran TrippierMidfielders: Joelinton, Sandro Tonali, Jacob RamseyForwards: Harvey Barnes, Anthony Gordon, Anthony ElangaWhere to Watch FC Barcelona vs Newcastle United - 2nd Leg Champions League Round of 16The second leg of FC Barcelona vs Newcastle United in the Champions League Round of 16 will kick off at 1:45 p.m. ET/ 10:45 a.m. PT in the United States.The match will kick off at 6:45 p.m. local time at Spotify Camp Nou in Barcelona, Spain. The match will be available to watch through select TV channels and streaming services in the U.S. and in other countries.Paramount+ (USA)TUDN (USA)UniMas (USA)ViX (USA)Amazon Prime Video (UK)TNT (UK)Movistar (Spain)Orange (Spain)Prediction: FC Barcelona 3-1 Newcastle United (FC Barcelona 4-2 Newcastle United Aggregate Score) FC Barcelona Advances to Champions League QuarterfinalsThis story was originally published by Athlon Sports on Mar 18, 2026, where it first appeared in the Soccer section. Add Athlon Sports as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
